core sudo_runner ETXTBSY flake[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Fix and close the five next-costliest open task beads, then [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]continue the backlog chain under the same ranking and closeout [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]rules.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]1[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] wave[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_backlog_epic_5.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/task_backlog_epic_5.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/task_backlog_epic_4.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1qt[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1qt/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the apollo-only ACE prompt-render and hint failures [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1ia, sase-1l3, sase-1hy)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]apollo-prompt-render[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]apollo-prompt-render: the ACE prompt-render and hint widget tests behind[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-1ia, sase-1l3 and sase-1hy fail deterministically on apollo (7-9 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failed of 30 across four files at sase 31a28d9618) and pass 30/30 on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]athena. Bisect the apollo host input that changes the result, fix it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]where it is owned (test isolation or product code), and prove the four [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]files pass on both hosts without weakening an assertion.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the agents-sync bounded-drain publication flake (sase-xo)[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]agents-sync-drain-flake[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]agents-sync-drain-flake: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests/agents_sync/test_commit_publication_bounded_drain.py::test_blocked[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]_render_is_bounded_and_leaves_the_request_queued still fails in loaded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]full lanes after the 1a69c8947d/4adee846d3 fix (recurrences 2026-10-27 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and 2026-10-31; one report measured 15.63s after git index-lock [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]backoff). Find what still consumes the wall-clock budget under load and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fix it without raising the elapsed bound or dropping the queued-request [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]assertion.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the sase-core sudo_runner ETXTBSY fixture flake (sase-15h)[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-sudo-runner-etxtbsy[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-sudo-runner-etxtbsy: in sase-core, sase_gateway sudo_runner tests [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]intermittently fail with ETXTBSY (os error 26) when exec'ing fixture [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scripts under the parallel core check (+7, latest 2026-10-31). Confirm [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the fork-inherited write-fd race on freshly written fixture executables [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and fix the fixture so no test can exec a script while any process still[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]holds it open for writing, keeping every sudo_runner assertion.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1qt","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-astra","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1qt.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-1qt.1"},"source_run_id":"run-1262d0a6113c1855965c7f00351bfc55","started_at":"2026-11-01T23:12:01.502039+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historica